description:
Port the template's encode.rs FfmpegCapability runner wrapper (x264 -crf/-preset/-tune animation; NVENC -cq/p7/-gpu, never the x264 preset; AAC -b:a 256k added once to the mux; timeouts only raised) with its argv-contract tests. Add (plan §3.3, engine review F-15/F-23):
- a camera-route wrapper around fmn::rendering::render_camera that installs the SAME runner-wrapped capability and encoder argv as the retained route (render_camera installs no ffmpeg; a camera segment encoded differently corrupts the stream-copy join);
- RenderOptions defaults raising max_output_bytes to 256 GiB and ffmpeg_limits.max_artifact_bytes to 32 GiB (85 s chapters stay editorial pacing, not a safety margin);
- the runner wrapper also captures fmn's s16 soundtrack.wav from the mux step's work dir (for the PCM master's null test, bead W2-master).

Tests: every argv rewrite pinned (port the template's 7 tests + new ones for the capture hook); both routes produce identical encoder argv for the same settings.
Credit rules (AGENTS.md "Honest Credit"): real code and real tests in the same unit of work; no mocks or recorded fixtures presented as live proof; never weaken an assertion or regenerate a golden to get green; close only with evidence bound to a commit.

Reusable components (plan §3.3 `props` row), each a small builder with a doc comment saying which idea it carries:
- proportion bar; histogram that grows from data (grow_from_edge per bar); equation card; verdict box; bit row with place values; prediction card (question held 1.5-3 s, with a fixed two-note sting hook for the score);
- ROW-STRIP heat map / table: one multi-subpath VMobject per row with per-point fill_rgba, recoloured in place by an updater (never 65,536 separate mobjects; never always_redraw);
- particle swarm: one v_group built at the origin and shifted, one group dt updater, placement-only motion (shift/rotate; a tail can be a child rotated by placement), never point rewrites;
- glow helper over v_highlight (8-12 layers, low source opacity, bright core);
- "for programmers" code panel sliding in from the right; "precisely:" lower-third; receipts card; names-to-search lower-third (plan §5.1 rules 11, 24, 26).
Video-specific props (space-time lanes, progress square, danger meter, seesaw, byte clock) live in their explainer crates unless a second video needs them.

Tests: builders produce the expected family sizes; the row-strip table recolours without changing mobject count across 100 updater ticks (planted negative: an always_redraw version grows the arena).
Credit rules (AGENTS.md "Honest Credit"): real code and real tests in the same unit of work; no mocks or recorded fixtures presented as live proof; never weaken an assertion or regenerate a golden to get green; close only with evidence bound to a commit.
